Coded the single gun-policy row for Matt Pierce and wrote it to `coder-2.json`.

His Nay vote on HB 1296 (2022) is his only evidence, but the bill bundles unrelated matters (police training, theft classification, juvenile jurisdiction, zoning) alongside the carry-license repeal — a multi-subject bill. Per V4.1, a No vote on a multi-subject bill proves nothing, so the row is BLANK (`no-evidence`), with a note in `needs_source` for a statement tying his vote to the specific provision.
